  "question": "For $$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix},$$ calculate $A+A^T$ and show that the resulting matrix is symmetric.",
  "answeroption": "A",
  "explanation": "<b>Transpose of $A$</b><br>$$A^T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Addition</b><br>$$A+A^T=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Symmetry verification</b><br>Let $S=A+A^T$. Then $$S^T=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix}=S$$<br>Hence, $A+A^T$ is symmetric.",
  "explanation_image": [],
  "options": {
